## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-time multi-tenant deployment, latency budgets, privacy guarantees, and drift monitoring in production-like settings.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time multi-tenant inference
- Early-exit and mixed-precision optimization
- DP/FL privacy guarantees and secure aggregation
- Drift detection and rollout strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference skeleton for two-tower model
function twoTowerInfer(input, tenantId, model) {
  // shared backbone
  const shared = model.backbone.extract(input.features)
  // tenant-specific embedding
  const emb = model.tenantEmbeddings[tenantId](input.userId)
  // combine and head with early exit
  const fused = concatenate(shared, emb)
  return model.heads[0](fused) // early exit path
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to handle new tenants with cold-start data? 
- How to quantify privacy-utility trade-offs with DP/Secure Aggregation?

## Why This Is Asked

Production ML systems must adapt to concept drift and data skew without sacrificing stability. This question probes concrete, actionable strategies beyond theory.

## Key Concepts

- Concept drift detection
- Sliding window retraining
- Score calibration and monitoring
- Safe deployment and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal drift check sketch (conceptual)
function detectDrift(scores, windowSize, threshold) {
  const w = scores.slice(-windowSize);
  const mean = w.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/w.length;
  return Math.abs(mean - 0.5) > threshold;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the rollback path before production deployment?
- Which telemetry would you collect to prove drift handling works?

